TASK-372 (parked, not applied): the error page names and Reload retries the URL a
failed provisional navigation was loading when the error itself names none.

- BrowserTab: records webView.url at didStartProvisionalNavigation (WebKit has
  already set it to the target there), clears it on commit, and uses it when the
  error has no NSURLErrorFailingURLErrorKey. WebKit's extension scheme handler
  refuses a main-frame load with an NSError whose userInfo is nil.
- NavigationFailureURLTests: five tests (script, link, tabs.update, background
  tab, Reload) against a refused webkit-extension:// page; all five fail without
  the BrowserTab change and pass with it (2026-11-16, 15/15 with the probes).
- testProbeA/testProbeB (print PROBE372 lines, assert nothing): why it is parked.
  A tab whose url is a webkit-extension:// URL wakes into that extension's own
  configuration (BrowserTab.wakeConfiguration), so after sleep + wake, Reload
  loads the page WebKit refused, even a non-web-accessible one (options.html).
  ProbeA (window.open child) shows it on main without this patch; ProbeB (script
  navigation) shows the patch extends it to every page-started navigation.

Known gaps if adopted (from /code-review, 2026-11-16): provisionalURL is not
updated on didReceiveServerRedirectForProvisionalNavigation, so a keyless failure
after a redirect would name the pre-redirect URL; the probes must be dropped, not
committed; testReloadRetriesARefusedExtensionPage, like the existing
testReloadRetriesTheURLThatFailed, waits on an error page already on screen after
a fixed 300 ms, so it should wait for the retry's own navigation instead.

Apply from the repo root: git apply docs/harness/task372/provisional-url-fallback.patch

